Allwyn asks Brussels to review Austria's nine-month online gambling timeline

Allwyn, a shareholder in both Casinos Austria and Österreichische Lotterien, has asked the European Commission to examine Austria's plan to open its online market. Concessions could be granted from 1 January 2027 and take effect on 1 October, a window Allwyn calls "extremely tight". The EU standstill now runs until 7 December, and the Finance Ministry expects about 20 companies to apply.

